  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "JJ has an array AAA of length NNN. He can perform the following operation on AAA:\n\n\nSelect any LLL, RRR (1≤L≤R≤N1 \\le L \\le R \\le N1≤L≤R≤N) and for each iii such that L≤i≤RL \\le i \\le RL≤i≤R, set Ai:=Ai+1A_i := A_i + 1Ai​:=Ai​+1.\nJJ wants to make AAA palindromic. Find the **minimum** number of moves to do so.\n\nNote: An array is called a palindrome if it reads the same backwards and forwards, for e.g. [1,3,3,1][1, 3, 3, 1][1,3,3,1] and [6,2,6][6, 2, 6][6,2,6] are palindromic.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT — the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN — the size of the array AAA.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\dots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ denoting the array AAA.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the minimum number of moves to make AAA palindromic.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\le A_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 3⋅1053 \\cdot 10^53⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n6\n2 6 4 3 4 1\n2\n1 10\n3\n1 10 1",
        "output": "2\n9\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1: We can perform the following operations:\n\n[2,6,4,3,4,1‾]→L=3,R=6[2,6,5,4,5,2][2, 6, \\underline{4, 3, 4, 1}] \\xrightarrow{L = 3, R = 6} [2, 6, 5, 4, 5, 2][2,6,4,3,4,1​]L=3,R=6​[2,6,5,4,5,2]\n[2,6,5,4,5‾,2]→L=4,R=5[2,6,5,5,6,2][2, 6, 5, \\underline{4, 5}, 2] \\xrightarrow{L = 4, R = 5} [2, 6, 5, 5, 6, 2][2,6,5,4,5​,2]L=4,R=5​[2,6,5,5,6,2]\n\nTest Case 2: We perform the operation on (L=1,R=1)(L = 1, R = 1)(L=1,R=1) 999 times after which array becomes [10,10][10, 10][10,10].\nTest Case 3: AAA is already a palindrome."
      }
    ]
  },
